Whisper: package Whisper's security prefs

What: lists browser/defaults/preferences/0-whisper-security.js in the package manifest.
Why: the security features keep their prefs in their own file
(browser/components/whisper/security/0-whisper-security.js), so they can change without
touching 0-whisper.js; the package manifest names every default pref file, and one that
is not listed is left out of the package. The line sits apart from 0005's so that both
patches keep applying with no fuzz when either changes.
---
diff --git a/browser/installer/package-manifest.in b/browser/installer/package-manifest.in
--- a/browser/installer/package-manifest.in
+++ b/browser/installer/package-manifest.in
@@ -279,6 +279,8 @@
 @RESPATH@/browser/defaults/permissions
 ; Remote Settings JSON dumps
 @RESPATH@/browser/defaults/settings
+; Whisper's security prefs (browser/components/whisper/security/0-whisper-security.js)
+@RESPATH@/browser/@PREF_DIR@/0-whisper-security.js
 
 # channel-prefs.js has been removed on macOS.
 #ifndef XP_MACOSX
